  </div>
  <section class="chapter intro" id="intro">
    <div class="intro-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Shantanu Pawar / Mechanical engineering</p><h1>Grounded in physics.<br/><span>Built for beyond.</span></h1><p class="lede">I explore the physics that takes us further.<br/>From ion–surface interactions to the future of propulsion.</p><a class="text-link" href="#about">Meet the mind behind the mission <span>↗</span></a></div>
    <div class="hero-bottom"><span>ENGINEER. RESEARCHER. EXPLORER.</span><span class="scroll-hint">Scroll to launch <span>↓</span></span></div>
    <div class="vehicle-label"><span>THE FLIGHT</span><p>A little curiosity.<br/>A lot of thrust.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="chapter about" id="about"><div class="copy"><p class="eyebrow">The person behind the physics</p><h2>Hi, I’m<br/>Shantanu.</h2><p class="large-copy">A mechanical engineer drawn to the questions that don’t have easy answers.</p><p>I’m at PVG’s College of Engineering, Technology and Management in Pune, India. My work brings computational engineering, plasma physics, and materials science together to understand how space propulsion can last longer.</p><p>For me, building a simulation is a way of asking a better question. Then letting the physics answer.</p><div class="signature">Shantanu Pawar<span>Author of the Virtual Ion-Optics Testbed</span></div></div></section>
  <section class="chapter research" id="research"><div class="copy"><p class="eyebrow">Flagship research / VIOT</p><h2>Small interactions.<br/>Far-reaching<br/><em>consequences.</em></h2><p class="large-copy">A longer journey starts at the surface.</p><p>I created the Virtual Ion-Optics Testbed to investigate how carbon coatings affect erosion in the NASA NSTAR ion thruster. It connects the motion of a plasma to what happens when a single ion meets a surface.</p><div class="research-facts"><div><strong>36</strong><span>simulation campaign runs</span></div><div><strong>3 scales</strong><span>plasma · surface · material</span></div></div><details><summary>Inside the research <span>+</span></summary><p>The study compares molybdenum grids with graphene and graphene nanoplatelet coatings. Nanoplatelets reduced simulated erosion, while monolayer graphene introduced an additional erosion channel. Field emission remains a critical tradeoff.</p></details><a class="text-link" style="margin-top:28px;" href={`${base}projects/`}>VIOT is one of twelve — see the full project index <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="chapter approach" id="approach"><div class="copy"><p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><h2>Follow the question.<br/><em>Test everything.</em></h2><div class="method"><span>01</span><div><h3>Start with the physics.</h3><p>Understand the mechanisms before choosing the model. Plasma transport, charge exchange, and material response.</p></div></div><div class="method"><span>02</span><div><h3>Build across scales.</h3><p>Connect GPU particle simulations, molecular dynamics, and custom Poisson solvers.</p></div></div><div class="method"><span>03</span><div><h3>Make it reproducible.</h3><p>Trace each result back to its parameters, assumptions, and verification. Keep the unexpected findings, too.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="chapter contact" id="contact"><div class="copy"><p class="eyebrow">Back on Earth. Looking ahead.</p><h2>Every mission starts<br/>with a <em>conversation.</em></h2><p class="large-copy">Propulsion. Simulation. An interesting question.<br/>Let’s see where it takes us.</p><a class="contact-link" href="https://github.com/shantanu-research">Find me on GitHub <span>↗</span></a><a class="replay" href="#home">↑ Replay the flight</a></div><footer><span>© 2026 Shantanu Pawar</span><span>Made with curiosity. Grounded in science.</span></footer></section>
  <aside class="flight-status" aria-label="Rocket flight phase"><span class="status-dot"></span><span id="phase">Ready for liftoff</span><span class="phase-count">01 / 05</span><button id="motion-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Pause motion</button></aside>
</main>
<script>
import gsap from 'gsap';
import { ScrollTrigger } from 'gsap/ScrollTrigger';
gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);
const media = gsap.matchMedia();
let paused = false;
let context: gsap.Context | undefined;
const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#motion-toggle')!;
const phases = ['Ready for liftoff', 'Liftoff · finding direction', 'Stage separation · going further', 'Payload deployed · in orbit', 'Touchdown · a new beginning'];
function setup() {
 document.querySelector('#phase')!.textContent = phases[0];
 context = gsap.context(() => {
 document.documentElement.classList.add('flight-active');
 document.documentElement.dataset.flight='preflight';
 gsap.set('.payload', {autoAlpha:0});
 gsap.set('.solar-wing', {attr:{transform:'scale(.035 1)'}});
 gsap.set('.solar-tip', {attr:{transform:'scale(.02 1)'}});
 gsap.set('.leg-left', {attr:{transform:'rotate(155 116 452)'}});
 gsap.set('.leg-right', {attr:{transform:'rotate(-155 184 452)'}});
 // Fixed nozzle translation stays on the parent; only local exhaust length changes.
 gsap.set('.booster-exhaust, .upper-exhaust', {attr:{transform:'scale(1 0)',visibility:'visible'}});

  const tl = gsap.timeline({defaults:{ease:'none'}, onUpdate(){
   const p=this.progress();
   document.documentElement.dataset.flight=p<.035?'preflight':p<.34?'ascent':p<.54?'separation':p<.78?'orbit':p<.975?'landing':'landed';
 }, scrollTrigger:{trigger:'main',start:'top top',end:'bottom bottom',scrub:0.65,invalidateOnRefresh:true,onUpdate(self){
 const i=self.progress<.04?0:self.progress<.34?1:self.progress<.54?2:self.progress<.8?3:4;
 document.querySelector('#phase')!.textContent=self.progress>=.8 && self.progress<.975?'Landing burn · returning home':phases[i];
 document.querySelector('.phase-count')!.textContent=`0${i+1} / 05`;
 document.querySelector('.flight-status')!.classList.toggle('in-space',self.progress>.38 && self.progress<.83);
 }}});
 tl.to('.booster-exhaust',{attr:{transform:'scale(1 1)'},duration:.08},0)
 .to('.rocket-wrap',{y:'-13vh',rotation:9,duration:.24},0)
 .to('.ground',{y:300,opacity:0,duration:.18},0)
 .to('.orbit',{rotation:35,y:120,duration:.5},0)
 .to('.sky-glow',{opacity:0,duration:.2},.15)
 .to('.flight-world',{backgroundColor:'#101c24',duration:.2},.25)
 .to('.stars',{opacity:1,duration:.15},.28)
 .to('.planet',{opacity:1,y:-60,duration:.18},.3)
 .to('.rocket-wrap',{rotation:25,scale:.82,duration:.18},.24)
 .to('.booster',{y:140,x:-32,rotation:-18,transformOrigin:'50% 50%',duration:.18},.34)
 .to('.booster-exhaust',{attr:{transform:'scale(1 0)'},duration:.04},.34)
 .to('.upper-stage',{y:-70,x:25,duration:.15},.35)
 .to('.upper-exhaust',{attr:{transform:'scale(1 1)'},duration:.08},.36)
 .to('.payload',{autoAlpha:1,duration:.04},.48)
 .to('.fairing-left',{x:-80,y:-25,rotation:-25,opacity:0,duration:.13},.48)
 .to('.fairing-right',{x:80,y:-25,rotation:25,opacity:0,duration:.13},.48)
  .to('.payload',{y:-65,x:()=>window.innerWidth<=760?-200:-20,duration:.12},.52)
 .to('.solar-left',{attr:{transform:'scale(1 1)'},duration:.055,ease:'power2.inOut'},.565)
 .to('.solar-right',{attr:{transform:'scale(1 1)'},duration:.055,ease:'power2.inOut'},.575)
 .to('.solar-tip-left',{attr:{transform:'scale(1 1)'},duration:.05,ease:'power2.inOut'},.605)
 .to('.solar-tip-right',{attr:{transform:'scale(1 1)'},duration:.05,ease:'power2.inOut'},.615)
 .to('.upper-exhaust',{attr:{transform:'scale(1 0)'},duration:.05},.53)
 .to('.upper-stage',{y:-320,x:150,opacity:0,duration:.1},.73)
 .to('.rocket-wrap',{rotation:0,y:'-22vh',scale:1,duration:.16,ease:'power1.inOut'},.66)
 .to('.booster',{y:0,x:0,rotation:0,duration:.16,ease:'power1.inOut'},.66)
 .to('.planet',{opacity:0,y:100,duration:.15},.72)
 .to('.stars',{opacity:0,duration:.13},.76)
 .to('.flight-world',{backgroundColor:'#ecece7',duration:.16},.76)
 .to('.ground',{y:0,opacity:1,duration:.1,ease:'power2.out'},.74)
 .to('.leg-left',{attr:{transform:'rotate(0 116 452)'},duration:.08,ease:'power2.out'},.82)
 .to('.leg-right',{attr:{transform:'rotate(0 184 452)'},duration:.08,ease:'power2.out'},.82)
 .to('.booster-exhaust',{attr:{transform:'scale(.8 .65)'},duration:.035},.8)
 .to('.rocket-wrap',{y:0,duration:.14,ease:'power2.out'},.835)
 .to('.booster-exhaust',{attr:{transform:'scale(.5 .14)'},duration:.115,ease:'power2.out'},.835)
 .to('.booster-exhaust',{attr:{transform:'scale(.35 0)'},duration:.025},.95)
 .to({}, {duration:.025},.975);
 });
}
media.add('(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)',()=>{if(!paused) setup();return()=>{context?.revert();document.documentElement.classList.remove('flight-active');};});
if(matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches){paused=true;button.textContent='Play motion';button.setAttribute('aria-pressed','true');}
button.addEventListener('click',()=>{paused=!paused;button.textContent=paused?'Play motion':'Pause motion';button.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(paused));if(paused){context?.revert();document.documentElement.classList.remove('flight-active');document.querySelector('#phase')!.textContent='Flight paused';}else setup();});
document.querySelectorAll('details').forEach(el=>el.addEventListener('toggle',()=>ScrollTrigger.refresh()));
</script>
